      "id": "r2",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "34. There are even others—Bṛhaspati chief among them,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "five or six in number, that are honourable ( enough ); but",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "Ráhu, delighting in ( showing ) his peculiar prowess ( or,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "showing his prowess against a distinguished adversary ), does",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "not act inimically towards them. On the new and full moon",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "days the demon-chief, whose head is the only remnant part",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "of his body, mark, friend, eclipses only two, the luminous",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "sun and the bright moon.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "35. S'esha supports the row of the worlds on his shelf-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "like hood; he is ever held on his back by the great Tortoise;",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "even him, the ocean consigns with little concern to the abyss",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "( of its water ); oh ! unbounded is the magnificence of the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "actions of the great !",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "36. Better would it have been ( for Mainàka ) to have his",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "wings lopped off with the strokes of the thunderbolt hurled",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "by the proud Indra, strokes which were unbearable on",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "account of the flames of fire proceeding thickly from the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "thunderbolt; but alas, for the son of the snowy mountain a",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "plunge into the waters of the ocean was not proper, when",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "his father ( Himàlaya ) was beside himself with pain.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "37. Since even the insentient sun-jewel emits burning",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "heat when touched by the pâdas ( feet–the rays ) of the sun,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "how can a man of mettle then brook an insult offered by",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "others ?",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "38. A lion, though young, attacks elephants whose ram-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "part-like temples are soiled with rut; this is the nature of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "the valiant; age, indeed, is not the cause of valour.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r7",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "39. Let caste go to the nether world, and let the aggre-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "gate of virtues sink lower still; let goodness of character fall",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "from a precipice, and nobility be burnt down with fire; let",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "the thunderbolt strike at once bravery which is no friend ( to",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
